From: VIDAL & ASTUDILLO Ltda <info@vidalastudillo.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Accept the setuptools_scm the distribution provides

python-dateutil 3.0.0 asks for setuptools_scm below 8.0. Buildroot carries
one setuptools_scm for the whole tree, 9.2.2 in 2026.08, and the PEP 517
build refuses to run when the pin is not met, so dateutil cannot be built.
The pin is dropped; dateutil only reads its version through setuptools_scm.

Upstream: none; python-dateutil still pins setuptools_scm<8.0 in 3.0.0.

---
--- a/pyproject.toml
+++ b/pyproject.toml
@@ -2,7 +2,7 @@
 requires = [
     "setuptools; python_version != '3.3'",
     "setuptools<40.0; python_version == '3.3'",
-    "setuptools_scm<8.0"
+    "setuptools_scm"
 ]
 build-backend = "setuptools.build_meta"
 
